`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"A sweep is many small scheduler jobs",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Week 6 gave you the strategies for a run that needs more than one device: distributed data parallel (DDP) and sharding. A scaling sweep needs them less than you might expect. Most of its points are small training runs, far below the size that needs more than one device. Each goes to the cluster's scheduler as a job of its own, and the scheduler runs many such jobs in parallel. Within-run DDP or sharding comes in only for a job that needs more than one GPU."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"That machinery does not tell you which size to train, how many tokens to give it, or whether the trained model is any good."})]})]})]}),`
