`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"MMLU-Pro names a question set, and the protocol is a separate choice",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["MMLU (Massive Multitask Language Understanding) asks four-option questions in 57 subjects ",e.jsx(a,{id:"hendrycks2021",children:"Hendrycks et al., 2021"}),". MMLU-Pro adds reasoning-heavy questions, removes noisy ones, and offers up to 10 options. Tested models scored 16 to 33 points lower on MMLU-Pro than on MMLU ",e.jsx(a,{id:"wang2024mmlupro",children:"Wang et al., 2024"}),"."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Option log-likelihood needs no instruction following, so it suits base models. Generated chain of thought fails whenever the answer takes a form the regex does not expect. The two cannot be combined, because option log-likelihood scores fixed answer strings and leaves no generated reasoning to score."}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["In lm-evaluation-harness v0.4.12, the MMLU-Pro task uses 5-shot generative CoT with regex extraction ",e.jsx(a,{id:"lmeval-v0412",children:"EleutherAI, 2026"}),". The course's tasks use log-likelihood protocols. For base models, the harness scores the full answer text as a continuation of the prompt. For Qwen3.5-2B, it scores the letter labels instead. When you report a score, pin the task configuration file or version and the dataset revision."]}),e.jsx(o,{title:"A bug fixed in v0.4.12",children:e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Release v0.4.12 of lm-evaluation-harness fixes a bug that placed the answers of few-shot examples in the user role when a chat template was applied ",e.jsx(a,{id:"lmeval-v0412",children:"EleutherAI, 2026"}),"."]})}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The exercise keeps MMLU-Pro because small base models are far below its ceiling, so saturation is not a concern. The goal is to study how the protocol moves a score, not to rank models."}),e.jsx(o,{title:"MMLU-Pro and the Artificial Analysis index",children:e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Artificial Analysis publishes an Intelligence Index, a weighted average over a set of benchmarks. It dropped MMLU-Pro from the index in January 2026 ",e.jsx(a,{id:"aa-index-v40",children:"Artificial Analysis, 2026a"}),"."]})})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{reading:!0,title:"Evaluation cost depends on protocol and precision",accent:6,number:"30",items:"4",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
